{
 "name": "noseat-pillar",
 "note": "Prices option B of decision kd-riXXp2Yvty (crabs eat elsewhere when no table). The decision states the A-vs-B fork turns on a growth-pillar cost it explicitly does NOT quantify. Today the sale is taken BEFORE the seat is looked for, so an unseated guest is already paid and fed; option B makes them a LOST COVER. Two arms model that, both on one tree so this is an A/B DELTA (kd-RSS4Nkil3c: a delta does not need an absolute re-base, but the control is re-taken here anyway as corroboration against the ruled 7/48). ub = --noseatsale, guest walks with nothing (no till, no rep, no need-cure) = STRICTLY WORSE than option B = an UPPER BOUND. fed = --noseatsale-fed, the crab is fed and charged elsewhere = the faithful option-B model. ctl = flag off, byte-identical to trunk. base-* = buy nothing, must stay 0/48 or the pillar reading is broken. batch sets kernel=wasm realm=main.",
